# AI Agents and Proxy Pools

A larger automation system may use a pool of proxies.

Conceptually:

```text
                Proxy Pool
          ┌────────┼────────┐
          ↓        ↓        ↓
       Proxy A  Proxy B  Proxy C
          ↑        ↑        ↑
          └────────┼────────┘
                   │
               Agent Pool
```

A controller can assign network resources to different browser workflows.

For example:

```text
Agent A → Profile A → Proxy A
Agent B → Profile B → Proxy B
Agent C → Profile C → Proxy C
```

This makes resource allocation easier to reason about.

