# Conclusion

AI browser automation is not just about teaching an AI how to click buttons.

A production-oriented system may need to manage:

* AI reasoning
* Browser automation
* Browser profiles
* Fingerprints
* Cookies
* Session state
* Network routing
* Proxies
* Geographic configuration
* Security
* Monitoring
* Error recovery

A useful mental model is:

```text
AI Agent
    ↓
Automation
    ↓
Browser Profile
    ↓
Fingerprint + Session
    ↓
Proxy
    ↓
Website
```

The most important lesson is that **browser identity and network identity are different layers**.

AI agents operate on top of these layers, while browser-profile and proxy infrastructure provide the environment in which those agents work.

Understanding how the pieces fit together is the foundation for building reliable, scalable, and maintainable AI browser automation.

